T express my thoughts, is all that I intend.
Your fable's clear; no rule you have transgress;
Cbast all your thoughts, yet nature still express;
Your numbers flow, as if the muses all
Consulted nothing, but their rise, and fall:
Your characters are just, and with such art
Your passions rais'd, they gain th' unwary heart;
And what you feign, effectually create.
Who was unmov'd at sad Felicia's fate?
Scarce cou'd the stubbornest deny their tears;
All felt your heroes miseries, as theirs;
But as a faithful friend, be touch'd me most;
By life's most noble, best of blessings, lost.
O heav'n, this my fondest wish decree!
Our mutual friendship may ne'er fatal be.

