Ill would it suit a female hand to wield The warlike weapons of the dreadful field. With daring steps to stride o'er heaps of plain, Or drive the flying Gauls thro' Hochstet plain.
Nor need we Marlb'rough's glories there display; Trust ev'n the foe t' immortalize that day. Tallard in bonds his triumph can't disown, And loft Bavaria, by his arms undone, Must tacitly proclaim what Marlb'rough won. Disabled France, to lessen Lewis' shame, Will gloriously record the victor's name. Let their proud chronicles with his compare Caesar's and Alexander's fame in war: Sing thou his nobler cause; the end alone Makes conquest great, and both are here outdone.
Fam'd Cesar Rome involv'd in civil broils; To sit aloft, tho' on his country's spoils : The other unprovok'd destruction hurl'd To unknown regions thro' th' affrighted world; Like restless infants, wept for a new toy, Of which he knew no use but to destroy.
